# NOTE: `go build -o pruefer` cannot place a binary at the repo root — the
# pruefer/ package directory already exists, so Go writes pruefer/pruefer
# instead (polluting the source tree). Build to bin/ instead:
#   go build -o bin/pruefer ./cmd/pruefer
/bin/
# Operator-local Pruefer runtime state: App private key, live config, lock, logs.
# Ignored wholesale — unlike .fabrik/config.yaml this is per-operator (App ID,
# watched repos) and must not be committed to a public repo. See cmd/pruefer/README.md
# for the config format.
.pruefer/
# goreleaser build output — must be ignored or Go's buildvcs stamps release
# artifacts +dirty (untracked dist/ makes the tree "modified" at build time).
/dist/

# verify-release-artifact's own build output (.goreleaser.yaml before.hooks),
# built before the release matrix — same reasoning as /dist/ above: if this
# were untracked-but-dirty, every subsequently-built binary would itself be
# +dirty because of this file's own presence.
/.release-tools/
*.exe
.DS_Store
tmp/
*.out
engine/.fabrik/
cmd/.fabrik/
tests/sim/.fabrik/
.fabrik/debug-footer.bin

# Old release-notes input file — superseded by release-notes/<version>.md
release-notes.md

# Operator-local docs: handoff notes, site/release runbooks. Contain paths,
# identities, and token-handling procedures — never publish to the repo or site.
notes/private/
SITE-OPS.md

# GitHub App credentials for engine App-installation auth (#1715). The private
# key, and the state file that carries the App ID/slug plus — for a fresh
# manifest-created App — its webhook secret and client secret. Unlike
# .fabrik/config.yaml, which is deliberately committed, these are per-operator
# secrets that must never enter history.
#
# `fabrik init` already adds both paths to .git/info/exclude (see
# writeGitExclude in cmd/init.go), but that is per-clone and does not travel:
# an operator who configures App auth by hand, or who clones fresh, gets no
# protection from it. These tracked rules do travel. The *.pem wildcard also
# covers a key placed at a non-default --github-app-private-key-path; no .pem
# is tracked today, and a legitimate future fixture can be added with -f.
.fabrik/github-app-key.pem
.fabrik/github-app-state.json
*.pem
